Note: switching to 'HEAD~1'.

You are in 'detached HEAD' state. You can look around, make experimental
changes and commit them, and you can discard any commits you make in this
state without impacting any branches by switching back to a branch.

If you want to create a new branch to retain commits you create, you may
do so (now or later) by using -c with the switch command. Example:

  git switch -c <new-branch-name>
---
1ee3a7f9 (HEAD) From Nathan Scott: - support for the version 3 PCP archive format - support for pmlogconf and pmlogger config file detection - tweaked output for #kmchart configs to reflect the tool that reads   them (the kmchart tool was renamed to pmchart ~15 years ago) - removal of some commented-out little endian lines (except in very   early development of the Linux port ~20 years ago, PCP archives have   always been big endian and we don't expect that to ever change now)
---
